<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Croton</h1><p class="st-meta">710 BCE – 277 BCE (approx.) · capital Croton</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Achaean Greek city of southern Italy famed for its athletes, its doctors and Pythagoras, which destroyed Sybaris in 510 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Achaean colonists led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myscellus-of-rhypes">Myscellus of Rhypes</a> founded Croton around 710 BCE on the Ionian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, reportedly on the advice of the Delphic oracle. It had a good harbour and a broad territory, and became one of the major powers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-graecia">Magna Graecia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Croton produced more Olympic victors than any other city in some periods, above all the wrestler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milo-of-croton">Milo</a>. It was renowned for medicine, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democedes">Democedes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcmaeon-of-croton">Alcmaeon</a>. Around 530 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythagoras">Pythagoras</a> settled there, and his followers dominated politics for a time before being violently overthrown. The sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-hera-lacinia">Hera Lacinia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capo-colonna">Capo Colonna</a> was a religious centre for the Italiote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>. After defeat by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/locri-epizephyrii">Locri</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sagra">Sagras</a> river, Croton crushed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sybaris">Sybaris</a> in 510 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 4th century Croton suffered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysius-i-of-syracuse">Dionysius I</a>, who held it from 379 BCE, and from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bruttii">Bruttians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agathocles-of-syracuse">Agathocles</a>. During the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhus-of-epirus">Pyrrhus</a> it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 277 BCE. A Roman colony was founded there in 194 BCE, and the town survives as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crotone">Crotone</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 710 BCE – 277 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.57%;width:8.62%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>710 BCE – 277 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Croton</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Achaean Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kroton, Crotone (ancient)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-494&amp;focus=croton" aria-label="Croton on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4933 595 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Croton lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5407 1012h0M5300 825h0M5383 1099h0M5304 942h0M5412 1053h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5253 851h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5253 851h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=-494&amp;focus=croton">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

